    {{ ('# ' + project_name + ' — data exploration') | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "First pass over the data: load it, look at it, save a processed version for the\n",
    "training notebook. Shared code lives in `src/{{ package_import_name }}/` — as soon as a step is\n",
    "worth re-running, it belongs there and is imported back into the notebook.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "from {{ package_import_name }} import data\n",
    "from {{ package_import_name }}.config import FIGURES_DIR\n",
    "from {{ package_import_name }}.config import RAW_DATA_DIR\n",
    "from {{ package_import_name }}.config import ensure_dirs\n",
    "from {{ package_import_name }}.seeding import set_seed\n",
    "\n",
    "ensure_dirs()\n",
    "set_seed()\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style='whitegrid')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'raw data goes in {RAW_DATA_DIR}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load\n",
    "\n",
    "`data.load_raw('<file>.csv')` reads from `data/raw/`, which is gitignored and empty in a\n",
    "fresh clone — so this cell builds a small synthetic frame instead. Replace it with the real\n",
    "load once there is data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "frame = pd.DataFrame(\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        'feature_a': np.random.normal(size=500),\n",
    "        'feature_b': np.random.gamma(2.0, size=500),\n",
    "        'group': np.random.choice(['control', 'treatment'], size=500),\n",
    "    }\n",
    ")\n",
    "frame['target'] = (frame['feature_a'] + 0.5 * frame['feature_b'] > 1.5).astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "# frame = data.load_raw('dataset.csv')\n",
    "frame.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Inspect\n",
    "\n",
    "Shape, missing values and label balance, before any modelling decision."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(frame.shape)\n",
    "print(frame.isna().sum())\n",
    "print(frame['target'].value_counts(normalize=True))\n",
    "frame.describe()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Visualise\n",
    "\n",
    "Figures go to `reports/figures/` (gitignored): they are outputs, and they are regenerated by\n",
    "re-running the notebook."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(11, 4))\n",
    "sns.histplot(data=frame, x='feature_a', hue='target', ax=axes[0])\n",
    "sns.boxplot(data=frame, x='group', y='feature_b', ax=axes[1])\n",
    "fig.tight_layout()\n",
    "fig.savefig(FIGURES_DIR / 'exploration.png', dpi=120)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Save a processed version\n",
    "\n",
    "`02-train-model.ipynb` reads this file, so both notebooks always agree on the features."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "path = data.save_processed(frame, 'dataset.parquet')\n",
    "print(f'wrote {path}')"
   ]
  }
